{
  "_comment": [
    "The typological questionnaire (Nekh-approved 2026-08-28). One profile per",
    "shipped language, SAME axes for every language, answered from linguistic",
    "fact BOUNDED BY THIS APP'S CORPUS: an axis is true when the beginner",
    "128-template corpus needs the behaviour to read as native (fr 'bel' before",
    "vowels is real French but absent from the corpus's adjective set, so fr",
    "apocope stays false). validate-language-profiles.mjs fails the build when",
    "a language has no profile, and reports every true axis that is not on the",
    "books in language_rules.mjs (declared feature or row flag). This is the",
    "check that makes 'nobody thought to mention Korean has particles'",
    "impossible: the question is always asked. Whether a declared need is",
    "IMPLEMENTED is the coverage matrix's job (validate-grammar-coverage) —",
    "this file only guarantees the need is declared.",
    "Axes:",
    "  definiteArticles       noun phrases take a definite article (the/le/الـ)",
    "  indefiniteArticles     noun phrases take an indefinite article (a/un)",
    "  nounCaseOnObjects      direct objects change form (or their marker does)",
    "  prepositionalCase      adpositions govern a case on the noun",
    "  verbPersonConjugation  verbs change by person/number",
    "  verbGenderAgreement    verbs agree with the subject's gender",
    "  grammaticalGender      nouns carry gender that agreement depends on",
    "  adjectiveAgreement     attributive adjectives agree with their noun",
    "  classifiersOrCounters  counting needs a measure word/counter (本/권/เล่ม)",
    "  topicOrCaseParticles   grammatical particles mark topic/subject/object",
    "  zeroOrSuffixalCopula   present-tense 'to be' is dropped or a suffix",
    "  pluralInflection       countable nouns inflect for number",
    "  spacelessScript        words join without spaces",
    "  apocope                some adjectives shorten pre-nominally (buen/gran)",
    "  politenessRegisters    grammaticalized speech levels (해요체/です·ます)",
    "  numeralInteraction     numbers change the noun's form or agree with it",
    "  specialPossession      'to have' is not a plain transitive verb",
    "                         (existential/suffix/enclitic possession)"
  ],
